# VTID-03928 — commands run during this change

## Investigation
$ grep -n "writeDevMemory\|write_dev_memory" -r services/gateway/src/services/*.ts services/gateway/src/routes/*.ts | grep -v dev-agent-memory.ts
-> only orb-live.ts's unrelated writeDevMemoryItem (different module,
   orb-memory-bridge.ts) — confirmed writeDevMemory (dev-agent-memory.ts)
   is called from nowhere in the live Operator path.

$ SELECT count(*) FROM dev_agent_memory;  -- via Supabase MCP
-> 26 rows, all source='backfill' (confirmed via a follow-up SELECT).

Confirmed the read side already works correctly against real staging
traffic before writing any code: ran `recall_dev_memory(p_query_embedding
:= (SELECT embedding FROM dev_agent_memory WHERE vtid='VTID-03817'...))`
directly — self-match similarity 1.0, related rows ranked 0.57/0.43/...
descending. The relevance-selection mechanism the platform owner asked
for already exists; only the write side was missing.

## Fix
Added `recordSessionOutcomeMemory()` to services/gateway/src/routes/operator.ts,
called fire-and-forget (`.catch()`, never awaited inline) right before the
/chat handler's response is sent. Writes a `task_outcome` dev_agent_memory
row for: (a) a non-duplicate created task, (b) any SIGNIFICANT_OUTCOME_TOOLS
tool call whose response.ok === true.

